title: what I read on planning, reviewing, building and working together, and what I took from each
pid: b034bd82-6ed1-48cb-81d5-d492db9209b3
body: |2-
  Read on 2026-11-13, in two missions, for [[id:6b88547d-78a8-4a64-a7e7-b754b201d97a][the planning procedure]] and the rule on when a second specialist joins a plan.
  Each headline is the source and the claim I took; its body is the
  address, how I read it, and more. The sources on planning come
  first; those on reviewing code and on working together are grouped
  after them. How I read each: "read" means its own words, through the
  fetch tool; "abstract" that I read only the abstract; "summary" that
  I read someone else's account of it; "unchecked" marks a figure I
  took from a search result without opening a page that states it.
  Quotes are as the fetch tool gave them; I did not check them against
  a second copy, except Bezos 2015, which I read in the SEC filing.
